Some amendments:

1=2E If the LINES environment variable is set appropriately before unix
nethack starts, then you can indeed use the larger screen size for long
inventory listings, options listings, ^P history, etc. Also works with
the win32 tty port (which will read the number of lines from the actual
console window size, not the LINES variable).
2=2E The in-game map is, of course, fixed as Kristoffer said. However, if
you have a *smaller* screen than normal, both the unix and win32 ports
will pan the map around as you move. This is an excellent alternative
to super-tiny fonts when playing on a PDA. (Now if only I had a
terminal app that supports color...)
3=2E When you set the terminal size in putty *before connecting*, NAO
*will* read the LINES variable supplied by putty and use it. So you'll
get the long inventory listings etc. as described in 1. (I just tried
this, and it works.)



